    "roles": ["band_member", "percussionist", "educator", "author"],
    "summary": "The drummer who turned songo into a defining sound of modern Cuban music. In Los Van Van he restored cymbals to Blas Egües' original kit idea, then added timbales and electronic drums, playing bongó bell and timbale parts at once and bringing snare-drum rudiments into conga and timbale technique. One of the most imitated Cuban percussionists and a teacher of Giovanni Hidalgo, Karl Perazzo and Luis Conte."
